  "human_edit_summary": "Round 2 of attempt 3, after the human remediation of round 1's four reviewer-B Majors. Round 1 closed with task-reviewer-a PASS 14/14 and task-reviewer-b NEEDS_WORK on TASK-SIZE, EDGE-CASE-COVERAGE, SCOPE-DISJOINT and DEPENDENCY-OVERLAP. The remediation landed in three commits: e28e12d8 recorded the chain predecessors T-002/T-005/T-006 had omitted, replacing each task's `### Blockers` value of None with T-001, T-003 and T-005 respectively (closing SCOPE-DISJOINT and DEPENDENCY-OVERLAP); 8d760af0 implemented the two 2026-08-25 human rulings, adding a Status:-based detection bullet for AC-006's clause (a) to design.md's SKIP Allowlist Activation Gate and to T-001's Scope/Done When, requiring T-005's validator to apply the two-clause predicate only for case_id AC-006, and recording an explicit Size Rationale for T-005 (closing EDGE-CASE-COVERAGE and TASK-SIZE); d9f1c42f restructured investigation.md's amendment record into a pure tail append so the workflow-state growth tolerance fires. tasks.md moved 0bd5df1d... -> 219a7a23..., design.md 4a2068c5... -> 14862a80..., security-spec.md 2918b235... -> 45adc9bd.... requirements.md, acceptance-tests.md, traceability.md, ux-spec.md, frontend-spec.md and infra-spec.md are byte-unchanged from round 1. This round's precheck was run with --provenance-rereview for one narrow mechanical reason: the previous persisted task-stage PASS contract (attempt-2/round-3) pins security-spec.md at 2918b235..., which the remediation moved, so check-workflow-state.sh failed fatally and refused an unflagged round-2 precheck; that stale pin is the sole cause (every other entry in that contract's manifest still matches the live tree, verified entry by entry). The flag's only other effect is requiring a prior persisted task-stage PASS, which attempt-2 round-3 supplies. Both reviewers were told explicitly that the TYPE-H provenance-rereview convergence rule does NOT apply to this round and were instructed to judge the current text on its merits under normal calibration; both confirmed they did not invoke it. Reviewer B received only integrated-summary.json (reviewer A's check IDs and counts, no narrative). Note for the record: attempt-3 round-1 persisted reviewer-a.json, reviewer-b.json, precheck-result.json, dependency-graph.json and integrated-summary.json but no integrated-verdict.json and no task-review-contract.json, so prior_round_contract_sha256 is left empty rather than fabricated.",
